  "description": "The proposed works include the following:\n•\tInstallation of 2 no. enlarged metal louvres for kitchen extract services within existing openings to North-facing windows to kitchen\n•\tInstallation of 1 no. new metal louvre within current glazed opening to South-facing kitchen windows (adjacent existing louvre, within original window frame)\n•\tBlocking and making good of 1 no. existing louvre opening to South-faxing kitchen windows (within modern plywood finish to window frame)\n•\tInstallation of 2 no. condenser units to roof of modern Dining Hall extension, Including associated pipework runs to connect them to kitchen ventilation system. Note - due to high roof parapet in this area condensers will not be visible from ground level within the site, nor from outside the site.\n\nThis work is in connection with with MEP works associated with kitchen refurbishment including new gas and water supplies, new ventilation ductwork runs. All pipes and ducts to run within suspended ceiling. No change of use is proposed.\n",
  "subdivision_of_building": "The proposed works are to affect the following parts of the school:\n-\tThe kitchen area and associated adjacent rooms, part of the original school buildings\n-\tThe 1954 nursery extension (ground floor now forming part of the Dining Hall, first floor remains in use as a nursery) \n-\tThe 2016 Dining Hall annexe including new WC provision\n",
